12227	{"artifactId":"LLD-3789fd85d0bbeb22-s1","entry":{"id":"review-62b639866c840d4c37d56b80cbffbd70","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-30T06:18:39.117Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design's enumerated capability categories (tool/MCP/plugin/hook/instruction canaries) correspond to the actual required-check set the collector must ultimately satisfy.","evidence":"src/shared/review-investigation-probe.ts:31-35 defines PROBE_REQUIRED_CHECKS = ['effective-inventory','raw-filesystem','shell','network','approval','cross-run','builtin-tools','user-mcp','project-mcp','plugins','hooks','repository-instructions','durable-progress','cancellation-exit']; the design's 'unexpected tools/MCP/plugins/hooks/instructions are failures' and per-category canaries (3.2/3.3) map onto raw-filesystem/shell/network/builtin-tools/user-mcp/project-mcp/plugins/hooks/repository-instructions. [files: src/shared/review-investigation-probe.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design states how the 'approval' and 'cross-run' required checks (present in PROBE_REQUIRED_CHECKS and the pre-existing ISOLATION_DENIAL_PROBES list) will be produced under the new control/restricted scheme.","evidence":"src/agent/providers/investigation-session.ts:29 lists 'approval' and 'cross-run' alongside the other denial probes, but neither the LLD's capability enumeration (section 3.2/3.3) nor its error paths mention how a canary or the control phase would exercise these two checks (they look like static launch-arg assertions, e.g. --permission-mode/--no-session-persistence, rather than canary-observable events) — the design never states this explicitly.","action":"Ask the author to state explicitly whether 'approval' and 'cross-run' remain covered by static arg/launch-digest checks (as today) or need a canary, so a reader isn't left to infer it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Claude native investigation currently uses buffered (non-streaming) JSON output, so host cancellation loses the startup envelope, as the migration's 'state before' claims.","evidence":"claudeInvestigationArgs (src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-session.ts:14-17) passes '--output-format','json' (not stream-json); CliProvider.runClaude (src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:599-618) only calls JSON.parse(out.stdout) after the subprocess exits, and rejects without parsing on non-zero exit — a cancelled run never yields an envelope. [files: src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-session.ts, src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing probe fixture writes its CLAUDE.md/hook/plugin/MCP shadow markers outside the real project discovery path (cwd), matching the claim that current canaries are 'inert' and not under real discovery paths.","evidence":"src/daemon/review-investigation-probe-fixtures.ts:79-88 writes filesystem-canary.txt, CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, hook-marker.txt, plugin-marker.txt and the fake MCP server under a sibling 'synthetic-config' directory of the probe root, never under `cwd` (the directory the native CLI actually launches in, built at line 34: `cwd = join(root,'cwd')`). [files: src/daemon/review-investigation-probe-fixtures.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The 'paired control + restricted phase' probe lifecycle and JSONL-frame native parsing claimed as new/changed do not already exist in the probe runner.","evidence":"src/agent/providers/native-investigation-probe.ts:37-124 performs exactly ONE subprocess invocation per probe attempt (input.invoke called once at line 80) and collectClaudeProbeObservations (src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-probe.ts:22-23) does a single `JSON.parse(result.stdout)`, not JSONL frame parsing — confirming there is no existing control-phase subprocess or frame-based parser to reuse. [files: src/agent/providers/native-investigation-probe.ts, src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-probe.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The claimed reuse of CliProvider, the provider lane, the probe fixture, and the export validation lifecycle is accurate — these already exist with the stated shape at the named call sites.","evidence":"createInvestigationProbeFixture (src/daemon/review-investigation-probe-fixtures.ts), acquireInvestigationProvider (imported in src/daemon/review-investigation-probe.ts:10), and validateUnsignedProbeExport/probeExportSchema (src/daemon/review-investigation-probe-export.ts, src/shared/review-investigation-probe.ts) are all real, already-wired components the design's call sites correctly point to.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The two documented function signatures (claudeInvestigationArgs, collectClaudeProbeObservations) exactly match the real code.","evidence":"src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-session.ts:10 `claudeInvestigationArgs(schema:StructuredSchema,modelArgs:readonly string[],cwd:string,indexed:boolean):string[]` and src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-probe.ts:13 `collectClaudeProbeObservations(result: ProcessGroupResult, identity: NativeProbeInvocationIdentity): readonly InvestigationProbeObservation[]` match the LLD's contractDetails verbatim. [files: src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-session.ts, src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-probe.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"An 'owned-root/file allowlist' exists in export validation that the design can narrowly extend for the new phase-evidence files, as 3.3 claims.","evidence":"src/daemon/review-investigation-probe-export.ts:26-29 enforces a hardcoded basename allowlist `['native-output.json','observations.jsonl','investigation-mcp.json','investigation-settings.json']` plus owned-root ('insrc-p-' prefix) and permission/digest checks — exactly the mechanism the design proposes to extend. [files: src/daemon/review-investigation-probe-export.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Older exports lacking the new optional phase-evidence/manifest fields remain schema-valid, matching the 'read as prior diagnostics, never backfill' edge case.","evidence":"src/shared/review-investigation-probe.ts:79-80 already defines `candidate: probeCandidateSchema.optional()` and `evidenceFiles: ...max(8).optional()` on probeExportSchema — the codebase already follows the optional-field precedent the design relies on for backward compatibility of new fields. [files: src/shared/review-investigation-probe.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"'Installed NativeIsolationEvidence remains unchanged' refers to a real, separate entity not among the design's listed call sites, so the claim of non-interference is structurally plausible.","evidence":"NativeIsolationEvidence is defined/used in src/agent/providers/investigation-session.ts and src/daemon/review-investigation-adoption.ts, neither of which appears in the LLD's call-site lists for 3.1-3.4, consistent with it being left untouched. [files: src/agent/providers/investigation-session.ts, src/daemon/review-investigation-adoption.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The new malformed/contradictory-stream refusal path is a natural extension of an existing refusal pattern in CliProvider, not a fabricated mechanism.","evidence":"src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:608-613 already catches JSON.parse failures on claude stdout and rejects with a reviewScoped-specific error (ModelResponseShapeError) vs a generic one — the design's 'bounded JSONL parser rejects invalid frames / unsupported version' builds on this existing distinction rather than inventing an unsupported pattern. [files: src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The claim of 'no automatic retry' for the probe path holds given the real control flow of the probe runner.","evidence":"runInvestigationProbe (src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:463-468) calls runNativeInvestigationProbe directly and bypasses runReviewSession's attempt/retry loop (cli-provider.ts:478-510) entirely, and native-investigation-probe.ts performs exactly one `input.invoke` call with no retry wrapper — consistent with the design's 'no automatic retry' invariant. [files: src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts, src/agent/providers/native-investigation-probe.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Each acceptance criterion (ac1-ac4) referenced in the acceptance-mapping table is itself stated (as text) somewhere in this document or an upstream artifact, so the mapping to tests can be judged for correctness.","evidence":"The LLD body contains no `acceptanceCriteria` field (only `testStrategy.acceptanceMapping` with bare `criterionId` strings ac1-ac4); `acceptanceCriteria:[{id,given,when,then,operationalizes}]` only exists on Define/Epic Story bodies (e.g. src/workflow/__tests__/head-naming.test.ts:69, :77-88 lldBody() has no such field) and this is a standalone LLD with no Define/Epic upstream (meta.standalone=true) — so nowhere does the document or any upstream artifact state what ac1, ac2, ac3 or ac4 actually assert. The mapping table lists tests against ID labels whose meaning is never written down. [files: src/workflow/__tests__/head-naming.test.ts]","action":"Have the author add explicit prose stating what ac1-ac4 assert (even informally, since the standalone LLD schema carries no acceptanceCriteria field) so the acceptance-mapping table is verifiable rather than only inferable from test-subject names.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The claimed test framework/reuse ('node:test with tsx; reuse native investigation and probe-fixture integration suites') points at real, existing test files.","evidence":"src/agent/providers/__tests__/native-investigation-probe.test.ts and src/agent/providers/__tests__/claude-investigation-probe.test.ts already exist and already test the collector/runner this design modifies, so 'reuse' is a real, not invented, claim.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":13,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-30T06:18:39.117Z","model":"cli-claude:claude-sonnet-5","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
