11724	{"artifactId":"LLD-3789fd85d0bbeb22-s1","entry":{"id":"review-02e1532d0d49a1ff3ce0c7cdedf368ab","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-30T06:31:21.520Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac2's canary checks (hooks/plugin/instruction/project-MCP) target a real, currently-unmet gap rather than duplicating existing coverage.","evidence":"PROBE_REQUIRED_CHECKS in src/shared/review-investigation-probe.ts lists 'user-mcp','project-mcp','plugins','hooks','repository-instructions' as required checks, but the current collectClaudeProbeObservations (src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-probe.ts) only ever emits 'effective-inventory','builtin-tools','shell','raw-filesystem','network','plugins' — no code anywhere produces 'hooks','repository-instructions','user-mcp' or 'project-mcp' observations today (grep found none). The new fixture in 3.2 is the right place to close exactly this gap. [files: src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-probe.ts, src/shared/review-investigation-probe.ts]","action":"Confirmed by reading claude-investigation-probe.ts and grepping for the missing check literals across src/.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Cross-run / approval checks that the design explicitly defers (edge-case table) rest on a real existing enforcement mechanism, not an unbuilt one.","evidence":"src/daemon/__tests__/review-investigation-probe-fixtures.test.ts already exercises the MCP bridge rejecting a mismatched runId/bindingId/progress replay (`forwardNativeReviewCommand` rejects on foreign binding/run identity) — the host-observed-rejection mechanism the design leans on for 'cross-run' is real and tested today, even though no code yet turns it into a PROBE_REQUIRED_CHECKS observation (which the design does not claim to add). [files: src/daemon/__tests__/review-investigation-probe-fixtures.test.ts, src/daemon/review-investigation-bridge.ts]","action":"Read the existing integration test and the bridge rejection paths it exercises.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Migration 'State before' claim: today's shared Claude launch (production + probe) uses buffered JSON output, not streaming.","evidence":"claudeInvestigationArgs in src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-session.ts:14 returns `['--print','--output-format','json', ...]` — no `stream-json` anywhere in that file or cli-provider.ts (grepped). [files: src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-session.ts, src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts]","action":"Read claude-investigation-session.ts and grepped cli-provider.ts for 'stream-json'.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Migration 'State before' claim: the current probe fixture writes its CLAUDE.md/hook/plugin/MCP canaries outside any path Claude would actually discover, i.e. they are inert 'shadow' files.","evidence":"src/daemon/review-investigation-probe-fixtures.ts:79-88 writes CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, hook-marker.txt, plugin-marker.txt and a fake MCP server config into `join(root,'synthetic-config')` — a directory that is never passed as cwd, never referenced by investigation-mcp.json/investigation-settings.json, and is not a recognized Claude discovery path (cwd or .claude/). [files: src/daemon/review-investigation-probe-fixtures.ts]","action":"Read createInvestigationProbeFixture end-to-end.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"claudeInvestigationArgs and collectClaudeProbeObservations, described in contract section 2 as being reused by both production and probe, already exist today with exactly the stated signatures.","evidence":"src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-session.ts:10 `claudeInvestigationArgs(schema:StructuredSchema,modelArgs:readonly string[],cwd:string,indexed:boolean):string[]` and src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-probe.ts:13 `collectClaudeProbeObservations(result:ProcessGroupResult,identity:NativeProbeInvocationIdentity):readonly InvestigationProbeObservation[]` match the LLD's declared signatures verbatim. [files: src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-session.ts, src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-probe.ts]","action":"Read both source files and compared signatures to the LLD text.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The 'new' active canary fixture (3.2: real CLAUDE.md/.claude/settings.json/.mcp.json/.claude-plugin placed under a discoverable project root) does not already exist — it is genuinely new work, not a re-description of the current fixture.","evidence":"The current fixture (review-investigation-probe-fixtures.ts) only ever writes canary files into the non-discoverable `synthetic-config` subdirectory and never creates `.claude/settings.json`, `.mcp.json` at `cwd`, or any `.claude-plugin` manifest — confirming no overlapping prior implementation to flag as a false 'new' claim. [files: src/daemon/review-investigation-probe-fixtures.ts]","action":"Compared fixture contents against the 3.2 description.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The call-sites list for the invariant-change in 3.1 (buffered→stream-json + native-only parsing) is complete — every caller that builds/consumes claudeInvestigationArgs or its launch digest is named.","evidence":"src/daemon/review-investigation-adoption.ts:98 calls `claudeInvestigationArgs(schema,modelArgs,cwd,...)` directly to build the PRODUCTION launch args, and line 101 calls `claudeInvestigationLaunchDigest(args,cwd)` to derive `expected.launchDigest` used for qualification — this is exactly the production/probe launch-digest parity the LLD's 2.1 postconditions describe, yet `src/daemon/review-investigation-adoption.ts` is absent from the 3.1 'Call sites' list (which names only claude-investigation-session.ts, cli-provider.ts, claude-investigation-probe.ts, native-investigation-probe.ts and daemon/review-investigation-probe-export.ts). [files: src/daemon/review-investigation-adoption.ts]","action":"Grepped every caller of claudeInvestigationArgs/collectClaudeProbeObservations and read review-investigation-adoption.ts around the call.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The listed call sites themselves are real existing files that actually touch this capture path, not invented paths.","evidence":"All five files named in 3.1/3.2/3.3/3.4 call-sites (claude-investigation-session.ts, cli-provider.ts, claude-investigation-probe.ts, native-investigation-probe.ts, review-investigation-probe-export.ts/-fixtures.ts/-probe.ts, shared/review-investigation-probe.ts) exist and were read directly, each containing the referenced functions/types (NativeProbeInvocationIdentity, probeExportSchema, PROBE_REQUIRED_CHECKS, etc.). [files: src/agent/providers/native-investigation-probe.ts, src/daemon/review-investigation-probe-fixtures.ts, src/shared/review-investigation-probe.ts]","action":"Read/located each file via Glob and Read.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Migration claim 'Older export lacks optional paired diagnostic descriptors' / 'read as prior diagnostics; never backfill' is consistent with how the export schema already models optional additive fields.","evidence":"probeExportSchema in src/shared/review-investigation-probe.ts:75-80 already declares `candidate` and `evidenceFiles` as `.optional()` on a `.strict()` object — the established pattern for adding new optional descriptors (the phase-evidence fields 3.3 proposes) without breaking older stored exports. [files: src/shared/review-investigation-probe.ts]","action":"Read probeExportSchema in full.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The numeric bounds 3.4 says are unchanged (≤300s attempt deadline, inclusive 128K token budget) match the actual current constants.","evidence":"src/shared/review-investigation-probe.ts:5-6 define `PROBE_ATTEMPT_MS = 300_000` and `PROBE_CONTEXT_TOKENS = 128_000`, matching the LLD's stated 300-second / 128K figures exactly. [files: src/shared/review-investigation-probe.ts]","action":"Read the constant declarations.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The 'unverifiable'/no-false-positive fallback behavior described for malformed or version-mismatched native output is already the actual behavior of the function this story builds on, i.e. the described error handling is a real, correctly-characterized extension point.","evidence":"collectClaudeProbeObservations (src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-probe.ts:18-27) already returns the `missing(...)` unverifiable fallback for an unsupported binary version, an over-limit/observer-failed result, or a stdout that fails JSON.parse or lacks a recognized `system`/`init` event — exactly the 'malformed/oversized/contradictory stream → unverified, no positive evidence' behavior the LLD's error-paths table describes extending to JSONL. [files: src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-probe.ts]","action":"Read the full function body and matched each branch to the error-paths table.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The test strategy's claim to 'reuse native investigation and probe-fixture integration suites' refers to real, existing test files that already cover closely related fixture/bridge behavior.","evidence":"src/daemon/__tests__/review-investigation-probe-fixtures.test.ts exists and already tests ordered durable ACKs, cross-run/foreign-binding rejection, and canary isolation from the real repo/auth; src/agent/providers/__tests__/claude-investigation-probe.test.ts exists and already tests collectClaudeProbeObservations's version/limit/malformed-output unverifiable fallback — both are genuine pre-existing suites the LLD's integration/unit subjects can extend rather than invented file names. [files: src/daemon/__tests__/review-investigation-probe-fixtures.test.ts, src/agent/providers/__tests__/claude-investigation-probe.test.ts]","action":"Located and read both test files' relevant test bodies.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":11,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-30T06:31:21.520Z","model":"cli-claude:claude-sonnet-5","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
