12826	{"artifactId":"LLD-3789fd85d0bbeb22-s1","entry":{"id":"review-ee38283406f0c60491ace16ff433c9e9","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-30T06:44:05.686Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac1 (preserve startup inventory through cancellation; native-only final parsing; unchanged ordinary completion) is addressed by a designed change, not left out.","evidence":"Section 3.1/3.4 and the error-paths edge-case table ('Production stream finishes naturally without exactly one valid accepted terminal result' -> 'Native-only final parser refuses; ordinary buffered completions and Codex remain unchanged') directly design ac1, and cli-provider.ts:115,244,358,427 show the separate non-investigation --output-format json call sites the design must leave untouched, which is a concrete, checkable target. [files: src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts]","action":"Read cli-provider.ts call sites for --output-format json outside runInvestigationProbe/runReviewSession.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac4 ('do not enable the engine or imply activation signoff') is honoured and no non-goal (automatic engine activation) is designed.","evidence":"Migration section 7 explicitly keeps 'existing engine selection unchanged' at every step, and section 3.3 states 'no candidate or approval minted unless all existing requirements actually hold... No signing keys', consistent with the already-shipped signing-key removal in commits d106c6883/fd31793e7/5ccd5c85f/97f3eb7ec that this story builds on.","action":"Checked recent commits per git log and cross-referenced migration section 7 and data-model 3.3 text.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Migration 'State before' claim: Claude native investigation and the probe currently use buffered (non-streaming) output, and the probe fixture writes canary files outside the paths Claude would actually discover.","evidence":"claude-investigation-session.ts:14 passes '--output-format','json' (buffered, not stream-json) and no 'stream-json' string exists anywhere in cli-provider.ts or native-investigation-session.ts; review-investigation-probe-fixtures.ts:81-88 writes CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md/hook-marker.txt/plugin-marker.txt/canary-mcp.mjs into a separate 'synthetic-config' (shadow) directory, not into the invocation cwd that Claude actually reads (cwd additionally has '--setting-sources','' disabling discovery), so these are inert/unreachable today exactly as claimed. [files: src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-session.ts, src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts, src/daemon/review-investigation-probe-fixtures.ts]","action":"Read claude-investigation-session.ts, grepped for stream-json/JSONL across cli-provider.ts and native-investigation-session.ts, and read review-investigation-probe-fixtures.ts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Claim that production review and the probe already share the same Claude adapter args/launch-digest derivation today (reference [[c1]]).","evidence":"cli-provider.ts:471 runReviewSession for 'claude' calls runClaudeInvestigationSession, which (claude-investigation-session.ts:24) is built from the same claudeInvestigationAdapter whose .args is claudeInvestigationArgs; native-investigation-probe.ts's runNativeInvestigationProbe also takes an adapter of this same shape and calls input.adapter.args — confirming the shared-args claim pre-dates this design. [files: src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts, src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-session.ts]","action":"Grepped runReviewSession/claudeInvestigationArgs/runClaudeInvestigationSession usage in cli-provider.ts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"claudeInvestigationArgs and collectClaudeProbeObservations, presented in section 2 as the target contracts, are existing functions (to be modified per 3.1), not newly invented names, and their current signatures match exactly what the LLD states.","evidence":"claude-investigation-session.ts:10 declares `export function claudeInvestigationArgs(schema:StructuredSchema,modelArgs:readonly string[],cwd:string,indexed:boolean):string[]` and claude-investigation-probe.ts:13 declares `export function collectClaudeProbeObservations(result: ProcessGroupResult, identity: NativeProbeInvocationIdentity): readonly InvestigationProbeObservation[]` — both signatures are byte-identical to the LLD's section 2.1/2.2, confirming these are reused/modified existing functions whose call sites (3.1) are correctly identified. [files: src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-session.ts, src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-probe.ts]","action":"Grepped both symbol names across the repo and read both source files.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"PROBE_REQUIRED_CHECKS / probeObservationSchema / probeExportSchema already exist with the shape the design builds its 'paired canary' extension on (observation check enum, candidate schema, evidence-file allowlist).","evidence":"src/shared/review-investigation-probe.ts defines PROBE_REQUIRED_CHECKS (includes 'hooks','plugins','user-mcp','project-mcp','repository-instructions') and probeExportSchema with an already-optional evidenceFiles array and candidate — exactly the reusable surface 3.3 extends with new optional fields. [files: src/shared/review-investigation-probe.ts]","action":"Read src/shared/review-investigation-probe.ts in full.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The call-site list for 'Bounded native Claude event capture' (3.1) and the file-allowlist claim in 3.3 point at real, exact locations that would need to change.","evidence":"All six listed files exist (claude-investigation-session.ts, cli-provider.ts, claude-investigation-probe.ts, native-investigation-probe.ts, review-investigation-probe-export.ts, review-investigation-adoption.ts) and review-investigation-probe-export.ts:29 contains exactly the four-item allowlist ['native-output.json','observations.jsonl','investigation-mcp.json','investigation-settings.json'] the design says to 'extend narrowly' — a concrete, correctly-identified change site. [files: src/daemon/review-investigation-probe-export.ts]","action":"Read review-investigation-probe-export.ts and confirmed existence of all six listed call-site files via Glob.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Section 2.2 postcondition that the collector must move from a single JSON.parse of the whole buffer to strict JSONL frame-by-frame parsing is a real, uncompleted change against current code, not already satisfied.","evidence":"claude-investigation-probe.ts:22-24 currently does one `JSON.parse(result.stdout)` over the whole buffered string and treats the parsed value as a single event or an array of events — there is no line-delimited JSONL parsing, no tolerance logic for 'an unfinished final frame on cancellation', confirming this is new work the design correctly scopes rather than describing as already done. [files: src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-probe.ts]","action":"Read collectClaudeProbeObservations body.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Adding the new optional phase-evidence/manifest descriptors (3.3) to the strict probeExportSchema will not break parsing of older exports lacking those fields.","evidence":"probeExportSchema (review-investigation-probe.ts:75-80) already uses zod `.strict()` with `candidate` and `evidenceFiles` both `.optional()` — adding further optional fields to this same object is additive and zod's `.strict()` only rejects *unrecognized* keys present in the input, so an older record simply missing the new optional keys continues to parse; this matches the migration claim 'Legacy diagnostic exports without optional phase descriptors remain readable.' [files: src/shared/review-investigation-probe.ts]","action":"Read probeExportSchema definition.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The edge-case claim that '--permission-mode dontAsk' and '--no-session-persistence' are current real flags, so the stated limitation ('--permission-mode dontAsk or launch digest alone cannot pass [the approval check]') is grounded in actual code rather than invented flags.","evidence":"claude-investigation-session.ts:16-17 literally passes '--permission-mode','dontAsk' and '--no-session-persistence' in the current claudeInvestigationArgs return value, confirming the edge-case table's specific flag names are accurate to the real launch args. [files: src/agent/providers/claude-investigation-session.ts]","action":"Grepped dontAsk/no-session-persistence/permission-mode across src/.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The 'budget, deadline, abort or daemon restart' error path's claim that the probe already enforces an absolute attempt deadline and drains child/broker before releasing the lane is accurate to current code.","evidence":"native-investigation-probe.ts:71-72 computes `timeoutMs = Math.min(PROBE_ATTEMPT_MS, context.deadlineAt - Date.now())` and throws if elapsed, and the `finally` block (lines 119-123) clears the monitor, aborts, and awaits `fixture.close()` before cleanup runs — matching the claimed drain-before-release behavior this error path relies on as a precondition to extend. [files: src/agent/providers/native-investigation-probe.ts]","action":"Read runNativeInvestigationProbe's deadline computation and finally/cleanup block.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The test-strategy claim to 'reuse native investigation and probe-fixture integration suites' names suites that actually exist.","evidence":"Glob confirms both src/daemon/__tests__/review-investigation-probe-fixtures.test.ts and src/agent/providers/__tests__/native-investigation-probe.test.ts exist in the repo, matching the named reusable integration suites. [files: src/daemon/__tests__/review-investigation-probe-fixtures.test.ts, src/agent/providers/__tests__/native-investigation-probe.test.ts]","action":"Glob for *investigation*probe*fixtures*.test.ts and *native-investigation*.test.ts under src/**/__tests__.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing collectClaudeProbeObservations unit tests already exercise the 'unverifiable on unrecognized version / malformed / over-limit output' behavior the ac1-mapped unit test subject claims, confirming the unit-test subject is a real, already-partially-covered behavior rather than an untestable aspiration.","evidence":"src/agent/providers/__tests__/claude-investigation-probe.test.ts:22-26 asserts `collectClaudeProbeObservations` returns 'unverifiable' for an unrecognized binaryVersion, non-JSON stdout, and outputLimitExceeded — directly supporting the 'Malformed contradictory unknown-version and oversized streams never pass isolation' unit subject mapped to ac1. [files: src/agent/providers/__tests__/claude-investigation-probe.test.ts]","action":"Grepped collectClaudeProbeObservations usage and read the matching test assertions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":13,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-30T06:44:05.686Z","model":"cli-claude:claude-sonnet-5","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
